Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.18 Text speed option in the text window

Every dialogue box, message box, battle report line and other typed message
gives its TextWindow a type delay of 6 (textWindowSetTypeDelay(win, 6)): the
window shows one more character every 7 frames. updateTextWindow adds that
character, textWindowDraw draws the visible part and runs the control codes.
The waits for a button (code 2) and the pauses (code 6) are control codes in
the text, state 2 of the window, and are not part of the typing.

The Text speed option changes only the typing, under PORT_HOST:

* Normal (default): unchanged. The patch only reports to the port; no value
  the game reads differs, so the default is bit-identical.
* Fast: textWindowSetTypeDelay turns a delay of 6 into 2 (a character every
  3 frames). Other delays are left as they are: the area name banner types at
  5 and stays an animation timed to its boxes; 0 (no typing) stays 0.
* Instant: the same delay, and updateTextWindow shows the whole page as soon
  as it starts (textWindowShowPage, the call Cross makes), so a page appears
  at once. It stops where Cross stops: at a wait for a button, a page break
  and the page's last line. The next line after a scroll types at the fast
  delay, and a pause code still pauses. Cross during typing still shows the
  page.

After each update the port is told whether the window is typing and whether
it is done (finished, or waiting for a button) so it can log how many frames
a dialogue page took to type ("dw3-pacing: text page typed in N frame(s)"),
which the replay tests check.

--- a/src/engine/text/text_window.c
+++ b/src/engine/text/text_window.c
@@ -1,5 +1,9 @@
 #include "engine/game.h"
 
+#if PORT_HOST
+#include "port_pacing.h"
+#endif
+
 /* The debug messages, in Shift-JIS */
 /* "Null message was passed" */
 const char STR_NULL_MESSAGE[] = "\x82\x6D\x82\x95\x82\x8C\x82\x8C\x83\x81\x83\x62\x83\x5A\x81\x5B"
@@ -392,6 +396,10 @@
  * Text window method: types the text out a character every `delay` frames (0 or less: all at once)
  */
 void textWindowSetTypeDelay(TextWindow *obj, s32 delay) {
+#if PORT_HOST
+    /* P6.18: the Text speed option shortens the dialogue windows' delay */
+    delay = dw3_port_pacing_text_delay(obj, delay);
+#endif
     if (delay <= 0) {
         obj->typeTimer = 0;
         obj->typeDelay = 0;
@@ -787,6 +795,13 @@
         break;
     case 1:
         if (obj->visible != 0) {
+#if PORT_HOST
+            /* P6.18 Instant: a page that has just started is shown whole, as
+             * if the player pressed Cross; waits and scrolls still apply */
+            if (dw3_port_pacing_text_reveal(obj->typeDelay, obj->finished, (s16)obj->visibleEnd - obj->start)) {
+                textWindowShowPage(obj);
+            }
+#endif
             if (obj->typeDelay > 0 && obj->finished == 0) {
                 if (++obj->typeTimer > obj->typeDelay) {
                     obj->typeTimer = 0;
@@ -827,6 +842,11 @@
         }
         break;
     }
+#if PORT_HOST
+    /* P6.18: log how many frames a dialogue page took to type (replay tests) */
+    dw3_port_pacing_text_poll(obj, obj->state == 1 && obj->visible != 0 && obj->typeDelay > 0 && obj->finished == 0,
+                              obj->finished != 0 || (obj->state == 2 && obj->substate == 1));
+#endif
 }
 
